From e932db36356bf014ca4154eec9530017ccbcd940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] fix(plugins): delete handlers read the current
 selection; transport errors are results

- handleProjectDelete / handleSessionDelete compare against the
  selection at call time (refs) instead of the one they were created
  with, so a callback held by a plugin UI across an await, or after its
  host unmounted, cannot clear a newer selection
- archive/delete actions return { ok: false, error } when the request
  itself rejects (no automatic retry of destructive requests)
- tests drive the real useProjectsState: a callback captured before a
  selection change keeps the new selection; rejected requests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
